m":"- [ ] Reconcile d278's seam-guard scope with the parent: either restore seam-guard deletion to parent AC6 (and the Measured-facts re-scoping) with a real referent, or strip the seam-guard title/ACs from d278 to match the parent's 'twin-merging only' decision.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4188,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent Measured-facts: \"'Seam-guard' has no referent. No `*_seam_clean_heldout.py` module exists anywhere in the tracked tree. `d278` is therefore scoped to held-out-twin merging only.\"","Parent child-decomposition: 'd278 ... held-out twin merging in the close phase. Independent, and narrowed by the seam-guard measurement above.'","d278 AC: 'The close phase deletes seam-guard modules created by the epic's split commits. Verified by a test.'","d278 AC: 'A seam guard NOT created by this epic is left untouched. Verified by a test, so the deletion is proven scoped.'","Repo search confirms no `*_seam_clean_heldout.py` module exists (only a historical docstring reference in tests/unit/test_logging_level.py).","container pairing: parent + 39bc-072e-9ebf-461d/6b48-37ea-a714-4545/d278-3792-6538-4c8e/d68f-4771-ebc1-4ee4/f86e-b57b-008d-4652/fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7"],"finding":"Child d278 contradicts the parent's explicit re-scoping decision. The parent's Measured-facts section states seam-guard 'has no referent' (no *_seam_clean_heldout.py module exists in the tracked tree) and concludes 'd278 is therefore scoped to held-out-twin merging only'; parent AC6 is worded purely as twin-merging. But d278's title is 'Move held-out twin merging AND seam-guard deletion', and two of its acceptance criteria require deleting seam-guard modules 'created by the epic's split commits' and proving a non-epic seam guard is 'left untouched' — scope the parent deleted and which targets artifacts the parent measured as nonexistent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32605f5a6df09752","impact":0.85,"is_primary":nu